# Goodreads API key — required by the Goodreads XML API (author/show.xml).
#
# IMPORTANT: Goodreads stopped issuing new developer keys in December 2020 and is retiring the
# API. Existing keys may stop working at any time (the API returns HTTP 401 Invalid API key).
#
# Local development: any non-empty value works to boot the server (e.g. `dummy`). The resolver
# then calls the live API and surfaces a clean GraphQL error if the key is rejected.
#
# Production bar: a real legacy key (when one is available), injected via your secret manager —
# never committed. The server fails fast at startup when this variable is missing.
#
# Future (planned): a BOOK_PROVIDER abstraction will add a key-free default provider
# (Open Library); GOODREADS_API_KEY will then only be required when BOOK_PROVIDER=goodreads.
GOODREADS_API_KEY=
